This is the standard fannkuch-redux benchmark. I use the usual algorithm, which generates permutations by rotation (the count-array method). The checksum adds the flip count for even permutation indices and subtracts it for odd ones.

The output is the checksum on the first line, then `Pfannkuchen(N) = max`.

Algorithm:
- Keep `perm1 = [0..n-1]` and a `count` array.
- Set `r = n`. Each iteration first sets `count[r-1]=r` in a loop `while (r != 1)`, then `r` ends at 1.
- Copy `perm1` into `perm`, then count flips: while `k = perm[0]` is nonzero, reverse `perm[0..k]` and increment the flip count.
- Update `maxFlips` and the checksum: `permCount%2==0` adds the flips, otherwise subtracts them.
- Generate the next permutation:
  - Loop: if `r == n`, finish. Otherwise rotate `perm1[0..r]` by taking `p0 = perm1[0]` and shifting the elements left.
  - Then `count[r]--`. If it is still above 0, break; otherwise `r++`.
- Increment `permCount`.

A single-threaded loop for N=11 or 12 is fine. N=12 takes a few seconds in JS with typed arrays, which is acceptable.

For N=1, the result is checksum 0 and `Pfannkuchen(1) = 0`. The loop handles this: `r=1` with `n=1` finishes after the first permutation.

```typescript
function fannkuch(n: number): [number, number] {
  const perm = new Int32Array(n);
  const perm1 = new Int32Array(n);
  const count = new Int32Array(n);
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) perm1[i] = i;
  let maxFlips = 0;
  let checksum = 0;
  let permCount = 0;
  let r = n;
  while (true) {
    while (r !== 1) {
      count[r - 1] = r;
      r--;
    }
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) perm[i] = perm1[i];
    let flips = 0;
    let k = perm[0];
    while (k !== 0) {
      let i = 0, j = k;
      while (i < j) {
        const t = perm[i];
        perm[i] = perm[j];
        perm[j] = t;
        i++;
        j--;
      }
      flips++;
      k = perm[0];
    }
    if (flips > maxFlips) maxFlips = flips;
    checksum += (permCount & 1) === 0 ? flips : -flips;

    while (true) {
      if (r === n) return [checksum, maxFlips];
      const p0 = perm1[0];
      for (let i = 0; i < r; i++) perm1[i] = perm1[i + 1];
      perm1[r] = p0;
      count[r]--;
      if (count[r] > 0) break;
      r++;
    }
    permCount++;
  }
}

const n = parseInt(process.argv[2], 10);
const [cs, mf] = fannkuch(n);
console.log(cs + "\nPfannkuchen(" + n + ") = " + mf);
```

